{
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-8%",
  "engine": "edge-tts 7.2.8",
  "duration": 166.25,
  "sample_rate": 48000,
  "channels": 2,
  "loudness_lufs": -16.0,
  "true_peak_dbtp": -2.41,
  "speech": [
    {
      "cue": 0,
      "start": 1.4,
      "end": 8.23,
      "text": "Each token leaves behind two vectors: a key and a value. One attention head is shown here.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/94a469542b93c547.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 1,
      "start": 9.15,
      "end": 14.68,
      "text": "Decoding appends another key\u2013value pair. The earlier vectors stay in the cache.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/ebbc1ecd52360b50.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 2,
      "start": 16.0,
      "end": 22.08,
      "text": "The next query reuses this growing cache to compute attention over the available context.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/1d9dd8d88d9167e6.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 3,
      "start": 26.85,
      "end": 33.23,
      "text": "Suppose each request reserves twelve token slots, even though its final length is unknown.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/93005d7e9ba8bc11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 4,
      "start": 34.133,
      "end": 39.833,
      "text": "Cut the cache into blocks of four. Allocate only the blocks needed by the current tokens.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/592d379909907533.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 5,
      "start": 40.733,
      "end": 47.623,
      "text": "The same fourteen tokens now occupy twenty slots. Only the final block of each request has slack.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/c9cb183ab812a452.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 6,
      "start": 50.483,
      "end": 56.783,
      "text": "A block table connects the token sequence to physical memory. Matching colors follow the same data.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/bcaf3c3ec55e20ed.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 7,
      "start": 58.233,
      "end": 65.323,
      "text": "For token six, divide by the block size. The quotient chooses a block; the remainder chooses a slot.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/326b3a9f7ce13906.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 8,
      "start": 66.233,
      "end": 74.533,
      "text": "Follow table[1] to physical block P2, then read slot 2. The logical token index is still six.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/77f6abf6bdbe21d7.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 9,
      "start": 76.45,
      "end": 82.93,
      "text": "The query compares with every valid key, even when those keys are stored in different physical blocks.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/8279d3754327dd72.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 10,
      "start": 87.0,
      "end": 94.08,
      "text": "Softmax normalizes all of these scores together. Physical block boundaries do not split the denominator.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/404b39562589ae2a.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 11,
      "start": 94.983,
      "end": 102.343,
      "text": "Use these weights to mix the value vectors. Paging changes storage, while preserving the attention calculation.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/01811adad378e40e.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 12,
      "start": 104.25,
      "end": 111.35,
      "text": "At six tokens, the request owns two blocks. Appending token six writes into an existing slot.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/4b2cb2586f336c95.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 13,
      "start": 112.267,
      "end": 117.207,
      "text": "Token seven fills the remaining slot. The block table is unchanged.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/723ab8e20f0d2ec4.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 14,
      "start": 118.117,
      "end": 124.187,
      "text": "For token eight, the offset becomes zero. Allocate a free block, then extend the table.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/6ea2c9b7a89bf727.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 15,
      "start": 125.1,
      "end": 131.16,
      "text": "After the request finishes, its unshared blocks return to the pool and can serve another request.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/f2046ae8fab5fbbf.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 16,
      "start": 133.067,
      "end": 140.457,
      "text": "Two continuations can share prefix blocks. Reference counts record how many requests still need each block.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/04bb0f6e56e8e478.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 17,
      "start": 141.367,
      "end": 148.397,
      "text": "A is about to append into a shared partial block. First copy that block; then change only A\u2019s table.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/b606533bf63bf619.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 18,
      "start": 149.3,
      "end": 157.07,
      "text": "Now A can write token six into its private copy. B\u2019s data stays unchanged, and the full prefix remains shared.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/c98f98402a42f2c9.mp3"
    },
    {
      "cue": 19,
      "start": 157.983,
      "end": 165.733,
      "text": "PagedAttention keeps token order intact while making GPU memory easier to allocate, reuse, and share.",
      "tempo": 1.0,
      "source": "audio/voice/3e18c55fb47ff04e.mp3"
    }
  ],
